{
  "description": "PR-07 segment 4: Relay's execution-surface decision and execution quota (DSHBox interlock-relay-core SurfacePolicy, CapabilityRegistry surfaces/backends, BackendDispatcher canServe/isImplemented, the three backends' supports(), RelayCoordinator handle (bring-to-front, requiresMode, isImplemented) and finishAfterGate (execRate)). 'registry' = allowed surfaces (registry order) and backend order per capability. 'decide' = SurfacePolicy.decide with the given preference / shell / sdk; backendCanServe is true except for the 'cannotServe' surfaces; 'surfaces' overrides the registry. 'stage' = the steps before the gate: decision, then E_SURFACE_MODE_REQUIRED, then E_NOT_IMPLEMENTED ('implemented' stands for dispatcher.isImplemented); 'json' is the text Relay writes on the device (libcore org.json). 'execQuota' = execRate after the gate with a fake ms clock: calls that went through approval are not charged. 'csharpOnly.backendMatrix' = every true backend:capability@surface for a set of device facts (the backends need an Android Context, so the JVM test cannot build them; the device shadow checks the registered capabilities).",
